    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d906">

                <pb facs="0828" n="712" xml:id="pg712"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/2693.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Ambassador to the Secretary of
                    State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1204.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-01-10">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 10, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to transmit herewith for
                    the information of the Department copies in original and translation of an
                    article which appeared in “El Diario Oficial,” the official organ of the Mexican
                    Government, with reference to the relations between the United States and
                    Mexico. I have to suggest the advisability of furnishing a copy of this article
                    to the President, as it may perhaps be useful to him to know that the
                    administration’s policy regarding the enforcement of the neutrality laws is
                    warmly appreciated by the Mexican Government and by its Executive.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Henry Lane Wilson.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d906-a1.xml" xpointer="d906-a1"/>
            </div>
